    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read the sentiment score",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "html",
        "content": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 6px 0\">Every headline (plus its summary) gets a score from <b>−1</b> to <b>+1</b> that says how <b>negative or positive its wording</b> is. It is computed by <b>VADER</b>: a dictionary of ~7,500 words rated by people (<i>“soar”</i> = good, <i>“lawsuit”</i> = bad), adjusted for negation (<i>“not good”</i>), CAPS and “!!!”.</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;margin-bottom:6px\">\n<tr style=\"opacity:.65\"><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">Score</td><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">Meaning</td><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">Example headline (29 Sep)</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">−1 … −0.5</td><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:11px;height:11px;background:#C4162A;border-radius:2px;margin-right:6px\"></span><b>Very negative</b></td><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">“Apple Faces a New Threat From Meta’s Muse” (−0.72)</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">−0.5 … −0.05</td><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:11px;height:11px;background:#FF9830;border-radius:2px;margin-right:6px\"></span><b>Negative</b></td><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">“Tesla Delays Roadster Reveal Over Severe Weather in Texas” (−0.38)</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">−0.05 … +0.05</td><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:11px;height:11px;background:#8E8E8E;border-radius:2px;margin-right:6px\"></span><b>Neutral: plain facts, no emotional words</b></td><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">“Company News for Sep 29, 2026” (0.00)</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">+0.05 … +0.5</td><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:11px;height:11px;background:#96D98D;border-radius:2px;margin-right:6px\"></span><b>Positive</b></td><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">“3 Reasons To Buy Airbnb Now” (+0.36)</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">+0.5 … +1</td><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\"><span style=\"display:inline-block;width:11px;height:11px;background:#37872D;border-radius:2px;margin-right:6px\"></span><b>Very positive</b></td><td style=\"padding:1px 16px 1px 0\">“OpenAI tried to invest $100 million in Hugging Face” (+0.54)</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p style=\"margin:0\"><span style=\"color:#FF9830\">⚠</span> VADER reads <b>words, not meaning</b>: <i>“MongoDB stock crashes 26% as its CEO jumps ship”</i> scored <b>+0.40</b> because its summary is full of upbeat words. Treat the score as the <b>tone of the text</b>, not a buy/sell signal.</p>"
      }
    },
